Input: {"question": "Which person or organization is in charge of maintaining Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 39, "text": "Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 41, "end": 223, "text": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds is an archival fonds held at the McGill University Archives, a repository of private archives and university records of McGill University."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 224, "end": 234, "text": "Background"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 235, "end": 245, "text": "----------"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 247, "end": 380, "text": "Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen (1875-1987) was a Norwegian-Canadian cross-country skier, ski instructor, and ski resort developer."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 381, "end": 519, "text": "He is credited with popularizing cross-country skiing in Canada and is often referred to as the \"Father of Canadian Cross-Country Skiing\"."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 520, "end": 677, "text": "Throughout his life, Smith-Johannsen accumulated a vast collection of documents, photographs, and memorabilia related to his skiing career and personal life."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 678, "end": 687, "text": "The Fonds"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 688, "end": 697, "text": "---------"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 699, "end": 843, "text": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds is a comprehensive collection of archival materials that document Smith-Johannsen's life and career."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 844, "end": 863, "text": "The fonds includes:"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 865, "end": 990, "text": "* Correspondence: letters, postcards, and telegrams exchanged between Smith-Johannsen and his family, friends, and colleagues"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 991, "end": 1098, "text": "* Photographs: over 1,000 photographs depicting Smith-Johannsen's skiing career, personal life, and travels"}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1099, "end": 1202, "text": "* Memorabilia: medals, trophies, and other awards won by Smith-Johannsen during his skiing competitions"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1203, "end": 1324, "text": "* Documents: newspaper clippings, articles, and publications related to Smith-Johannsen's skiing career and personal life"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1325, "end": 1422, "text": "* Audio-visual materials: recordings of Smith-Johannsen's interviews, speeches, and skiing events"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1424, "end": 1434, "text": "Repository"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1435, "end": 1445, "text": "----------"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1447, "end": 1617, "text": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds is maintained by the McGill University Archives, a repository of private archives and university records of McGill University."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1618, "end": 1736, "text": "The archives are located in the McLennan Library Building on the McGill University campus in Montreal, Quebec, Canada."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1737, "end": 1745, "text": "Evidence"}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1746, "end": 1754, "text": "--------"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1756, "end": 1934, "text": "* The McGill University Archives website lists the Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds as one of its holdings, providing a detailed description of the fonds and its contents."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1935, "end": 1938, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1939, "end": 2133, "text": "* The Archives Canada website, a database of archival fonds and collections across Canada, also lists the Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds as being held at the McGill University Archives."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2134, "end": 2137, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2138, "end": 2386, "text": "* A 2011 article in the McGill University News, \"McGill Archives acquires Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen fonds\", confirms that the fonds was acquired by the McGill University Archives and provides additional information about the contents of the fonds."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 39, "text": "Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 41, "end": 193, "text": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds is a comprehensive archival collection held at the Jimmy Carter Library and Museum in Atlanta, Georgia, USA."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 194, "end": 201, "text": "History"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 202, "end": 210, "text": "--------"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 212, "end": 382, "text": "The fonds was established in 1985, following a donation of personal papers and memorabilia by Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen, a renowned Canadian athlete and explorer."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 383, "end": 618, "text": "Smith-Johannsen, known for his expeditions to the Canadian Arctic and his advocacy for environmental conservation, had a long-standing relationship with former US President Jimmy Carter, who shared his passion for environmental issues."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 619, "end": 767, "text": "In 1982, Carter, then out of office, visited McGill University in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, where he delivered a lecture on sustainable development."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 768, "end": 853, "text": "During his visit, he met with Smith-Johannsen, who was a guest of honor at the event."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 854, "end": 1002, "text": "The two men discussed their shared concerns about the impact of human activity on the environment and the importance of preserving natural habitats."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1003, "end": 1139, "text": "Following their meeting, Carter and Smith-Johannsen began corresponding regularly, exchanging letters and ideas on environmental issues."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1140, "end": 1289, "text": "In 1985, Smith-Johannsen decided to donate his personal papers and memorabilia to the Jimmy Carter Library and Museum, which was established in 1982."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1290, "end": 1297, "text": "Content"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1298, "end": 1306, "text": "--------"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1308, "end": 1393, "text": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds consists of over 10,000 items, including:"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1395, "end": 1455, "text": "* Personal correspondence between Smith-Johannsen and Carter"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1456, "end": 1547, "text": "* Photographs and documents related to Smith-Johannsen's expeditions to the Canadian Arctic"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1548, "end": 1629, "text": "* Newspaper clippings and articles about Smith-Johannsen's environmental activism"}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1630, "end": 1751, "text": "* Memorabilia, such as medals and awards, received by Smith-Johannsen for his contributions to environmental conservation"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1753, "end": 1775, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1776, "end": 1796, "text": "--------------------"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1798, "end": 1870, "text": "* \"The Environmental Legacy of Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen\" by Dr."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1871, "end": 1919, "text": "Jane Doe (Journal of Environmental Studies, Vol."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1920, "end": 1927, "text": "10, No."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1928, "end": 1936, "text": "2, 1990)"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1937, "end": 2016, "text": "* \"Jimmy Carter and the Environment: A Study of Presidential Leadership\" by Dr."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2017, "end": 2065, "text": "John Smith (Presidential Studies Quarterly, Vol."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2066, "end": 2073, "text": "25, No."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2074, "end": 2082, "text": "3, 1995)"}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2083, "end": 2161, "text": "* \"Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen: A Life of Adventure and Activism\" by Dr."}, "D2S30": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2162, "end": 2208, "text": "Mary Johnson (Canadian Historical Review, Vol."}, "D2S31": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2209, "end": 2216, "text": "80, No."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "organization", "scope": "The Herman Jackrabbit Smith-Johannsen Fonds", "claim": "The Jimmy Carter Library and Museum is in charge of maintaining 